{"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLTied","kind":"identifier"}],"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"overview","text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The number attribute is rarely needed to disambiguate ties, since note pitches will usually suffice. The"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"attribute is implied rather than defaulting to 1 as with most elements. It is available for use in more"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"complex tied notation situations."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Ties that join two notes of the same pitch together should be represented with a tied element on the first"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"note with type=“start” and a tied element on the second note with type=“stop”. This can also be done if the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"two notes being tied are enharmonically equivalent, but have different step values. It is not recommended to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"use tied elements to join two notes with enharmonically inequivalent pitches."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Ties that indicate that an instrument should be undamped are specified with a single tied element with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"type=“let-ring”."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Ties that are visually attached to only one note, other than undamped ties, should be specified with two tied"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"elements on the same note, first type=“start” then type=“stop”. This can be used to represent ties into or out"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"of repeated sections or codas."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Maps the MusicXML "},{"code":"<tied>","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" element."}]}]}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL"]]},"kind":"symbol","identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLTied","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"relationshipsSections":[{"type":"conformsTo","title":"Conforms To","identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s8CopyableP","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/SQ","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s9EscapableP","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/SH","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"kind":"relationships"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxltied"]}],"metadata":{"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLTied"}],"role":"symbol","roleHeading":"Structure","title":"MXLTied","externalID":"s:7IvorMXL7MXLTiedV","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLTied","kind":"identifier"}],"symbolKind":"struct","modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The tied element represents the notated tie. The tie element represents the tie sound."}],"topicSections":[{"title":"Initializers","identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLTied\/init(id:kind:number:lineKind:dashLength:spaceLength:position:placement:orientation:bezierX:bezierY:bezierX2:bezierY2:bezierOffset:bezierOffset2:color:)"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Initializers"},{"anchor":"Instance-Properties","title":"Instance Properties","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLTied\/bezierOffset","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLTied\/bezierOffset2","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLTied\/bezierX","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLTied\/bezierX2","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLTied\/bezierY","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/